# Read by the test stage, which copies the tree in, and by the wheels and dev
# stages, which bind-mount Dockerfile.lock from the context. The .env files and
# Compose overrides hold this checkout's settings, not the tree's. Every
# top-level dot path is left out, so a per-user one such as .claude stays out
# without being named, and the project's own are let back in by name. A
# submodule under lib/ is a checkout too, with settings of its own, and nothing
# here reads its dot files, so none is let back in.
**/.git
/.*
/docker-compose.*.yml
/lib/*/.*
/lib/*/docker-compose.*.yml
/lib/*/tmp/
/tmp/

!/.dockerignore
!/.dockerrepo
!/.env.example
!/.github
!/.gitignore
!/.gitmodules
!/.hadolint.yaml
!/.yamllint.yaml
